### Try these from VS Code with the "REST Client" extension: click "Send Request" above each one.
### The app seeds policy id 1 (AUTO-1001, $10,000 limit) on first startup.

### File a valid claim
POST http://localhost:8080/api/claims
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyId": 1,
  "incidentDate": "2026-11-01",
  "description": "Rear-ended at a stoplight",
  "amountRequested": 2500.00
}

### File a claim over the coverage limit (expect 422)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/claims
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyId": 1,
  "incidentDate": "2026-11-01",
  "description": "Total loss",
  "amountRequested": 50000.00
}

### Missing fields (expect 400 with validation messages)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/claims
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyId": 1
}

### List all claims
GET http://localhost:8080/api/claims

### List claims by status
GET http://localhost:8080/api/claims?status=SUBMITTED

### Get one claim
GET http://localhost:8080/api/claims/1

### Move claim 1 through its lifecycle
POST http://localhost:8080/api/claims/1/review

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/claims/1/approve

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/claims/1/pay

### Try an illegal transition (expect 422)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/claims/1/deny
